Review the result of the task in <D>/.work/s/task-1.md against its done criteria (the work is committed on branch `job/t1` (worktrees: /w/r); full diff per repo: `git diff abc...job/t1`; leave the worktrees as they are. Driver test run: the script already ran the task's Test lines in the worktree after the dev's last DONE and they passed (a task with no Test line was not run); do not rerun them or the gate. The change as the script saw it (long diffs are cut, read the rest with the command above):
DIFF
). Before a FAIL on a 'still present' claim, quote the exact line from the current file. Predicted paths are a planning hint: a file outside them is never a FAIL by itself. First search for code with `lp find "question"` or `lp nav def|refs|outline FILE`; grep only to confirm literal text afterwards. Offload to the local model (no paid tokens): `lp judge|review` for criteria and diff checks, `lp bulk|pack` for long reads (see <R>/.claude/practices/code-nav.md). Never `cd <dir>` before git: use `git -C <dir> <args>` (plain `git <args>` when your cwd is already the worktree), e.g. `git -C wt status`. One `cs-qrun` call per Bash call: after it only `&& <another cs-qrun call>` or `&& <read-only command>` (ls, echo, wc, cat, head, tail, test), e.g. `cs-qrun -- pytest && ls out`. Read JSON/JSONL with `jq` (allowed, no approval), not python/node scripts: `jq -c 'select(.id=="sd-170")' f.jsonl`, `jq '.items|length' f.json`, `jq -r '.items|to_entries[]|[.key,.value.ok,.value.bad]|@tsv' f.json`; recipes: practices/bash.md. Scratchpad for temp files and logs: .work/s/tmp/ (write nothing temporary elsewhere; delete what you no longer need when you finish). Write your full report (files changed, test result, any ESCALATE line; for a review: counts and every 'wrong' item) to .work/s/reports/report-x5.md, its FIRST line `VERDICT: PASS|FAIL|ESCALATE`, then reply with exactly: REPORT x5
